title: One big chair or two small ones?
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Part of the form is to "compete" with other big lounge chairs. But yes, there are perhaps smaller and still "comfortable" chairs that could have been made, perhaps two smaller chairs per one big Oka Chair? Is that smart? Does that make sense at the price point and statement level?

The price point: $6,900 for one [[Oka Chair]], made to order. ([[okaterra.com|https://okaterra.com/products/the-oka-chair]], October 2026)
